{"kind":"report","text":"Approved as evidence-only design at exact R3 revision 9, 8b8f946d2b7e2e060f7a34ce76960eeee709448d, for the complete three-subject package under live f70b85b6 and ordinary invitation f33a6065. No new high-confidence material defect remains in the assessed subject set. This is independent design assessment, not implementation closure, executable adoption of missing common-contract forms, provider validation or operational acceptance. Every original f2d23e6f / current R3 condition remains.\n\nReading and exact binding: full current authority note, corrections and dated publication/authority facts were assessed through the complete prior whole-document readings and verified changed bytes, as recorded in preliminary report 0adeddd9. For revision 9 root read the entire unified-8 delta from fully assessed c9153f00: 67,730 UTF-8 bytes / 566 LF lines / 67,614 characters through EOF. Unchanged bytes transfer only through exact identity. Current ancestry is 8b8f946d -\u003e c9153f00; the prior v8 assessment covered its entire 61,340-byte / 583-line diff from fully assessed v7, whose earlier complete changes and unchanged reads are retained in da88fb08. The facts file is unchanged. All current filing records, live request, builder promise and invitation were read in full. Independent ancestry, replay and cost audits informed 0adeddd9; root separately verified the critical start/stop/carry/judgment/replay and pin/retention rules, freshly rereading main lines 1736–1886 and 2171–2245 while assessing R4's same-commitment control.\n\nRegistered clean detached checkout /tmp/artroom-checker-r3-8b8f946d-EVPftH/checkout holds this exact HEAD and no changes. All three files match frozen Git byte for byte. Main: 258,957 bytes / 3,111 LF lines, SHA256 d4e83dd78f1ad68110ebc9a399330dd2cfc468b972733c00d09f7a4ed7d8ad53, blob e3b3ddba42f934577103a62cf258a377df33298d. Corrections: 51,538 / 340, SHA256 30d45fed2d17d2a4585282e3cae654e787c6cc05f64064896424448c829dc4fe, blob c4ca17001cf54c0e5ce004eca65f56fc89948b79. Publication/authority facts: 84,111 / 723, SHA256 12db56d1ba4a9681e47408ebfc7cbfa75495163592a3e54bed4b85f71e76f8e0, unchanged blob ab371b65ffd5bc07e015f5172661fd9e9a559193. No facts page was fetched again and no count script was run.\n\nArchitecture: current authority/freshness, explicit observation identity/run/reuse, clamped non-time outcomes versus refused time judgments, durable attempt/outbox identities, commitment and reservation freezing, exact publication recovery and independent retained-input replay remain coherent design boundaries. The published-history repair is correct: a foreign start reachable from the recorded destination head needs no basis and is never in F. The branch stop is tried first; published carried commits are removed; replay derives the same judgment from the retained head, commits and staged-ref snapshot rather than current mutable refs. Published head reports remain possible while another lane retains its root. The unpublished foreign-start refusal, own-check/input basis ordering and full carried ancestry remain preserved.\n\nSecurity: a staged/live/provisionally pinned own root is not evidence of its own ancestry. An earlier admitted check or selected input is required for the corresponding stop; an own ref cannot mask a foreign ref. Source authors, selected/replaced provenance and independent reviewer exclusion remain part of the judgment. Unknown token, writer, create/push/publication and export effects remain duties until their own outcomes reconcile; a namespace listing, restart or replacement scope does not settle them. Disconnected and revoked principals remain distinct. Operational trust H1–H6 and provider fencing/custody contracts are assumptions with owners, not proof from retained bytes or fixture success. Missing required retained inputs remain incomplete.\n\nSimplification: the correction changes one ancestry judgment and its replay/control evidence, using existing refusals and recorded inputs. It adds no new protocol engine, Cartesian matrix, numerical test quota or fixed Jam gate. The reachable same-commitment unchecked-ancestor control recorded in R4v8 is a useful compact derivation from these rules: B on unadmitted A is refused; after A's clean report is admitted, a newly prepared B check can stop at A and carry empty F. R3's own witness table for that case remains an explicitly owned reconciliation item, not runtime proof.\n\nRemaining common-contract dependencies are preserved in full. O1–O10 and current R1 follow-through 1e85696d / f5a2d356 must receive actual dispositions for observations, freshness, preparation/ledger writes, sends and reserves, retained ancestry/authority inputs, validation and replay. R2's adopted base still pins the older start summary; its full successor cb523654 owns concrete forms and the published-start record. Required-check configuration authority, checker error/failed/timeout mapping and baseline Node discovery/listening at actual hosted/checker boundaries remain owed. U15 cross-lane export, H1–H6, undeclared forms and budgets, complete current writer/resource/config/agent sender successor-removal inventory, settlement of every unknown effect/credential, real/local/hosted/agent/device outcomes, cold public/manual/application acceptance and complete browser/device workflow remain required. Later expanded interfaces need their own normal review/adoption before dependent joint source; the agreed I1 primitives can continue.\n\nNonblocking cost qualification from 0adeddd9 remains: visited counts the parent walk; reachability from the destination head for branch/start/carry is not separately quantified. This is not an evidenced cap bypass or measured regression. R3/R4 retain actual work accounting, whole replay and whole install/setup/edit-to-review wall/CPU measurement toward the tenth goal without inventing a new bound. Estimates remove no functionality. Builder retains the first-Jam readiness judgment.\n\nStatic source/document/provenance review only: no tests, builds, installs, typechecks, probes, repository/package code execution, provider calls, source edits, pushes, merges, private diagnostic retry or reviewer/model/backend change. Approval binds all three exact filed subjects and preserves the full implementation and operational obligations.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:df4ee6c59f2d2911b12525aea1fdbbef65091df7","binding":"evidence-only","head":"8b8f946d2b7e2e060f7a34ce76960eeee709448d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:53924375e6d5c96069c3a77149331f76f02c0b44\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8f158813b362513b50187fcb3d57e40f95ead188","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}